(A `value` that holds a map when a `For each` begins: the error flag is set
 and the body does not run. A map's keys are walked by naming the map.)
a value called box is {"k": 1, "j": 2}.
For each item in box, print item.
On error print "the value holds no list".
a map called stock is box.
a text called names is "keys:".
For each name in stock's keys, Set names to "{names} {name}".
Print names.
